  "legacy_defects": [
    "retire and dissolve interrupt the target's turn before the transaction; a call refused afterwards (a self-retire with live reports, a keyed call refused at admission) has already interrupted it",
    "a keyed rename is executed without admission: a malformed op_key is not refused and no receipt is filed",
    "the retained-result allowlists of retire, dissolve, move, retool and swap name fields the result never carries as a scalar, so their receipts keep nothing",
    "the post-save remote reap names orgtree_rename, but the rename branch returns before it",
    "list_orgs is a read that takes the write lock, saves and broadcasts hub_changed",
    "dissolve-all tells each later top-level seat that an earlier one was dissolved, then dissolves it in the same save",
    "a move to the node's current parent answers its no-op before any authority check, so any caller gets an accepted write cycle that confirms the node's parent"
  ],
  "scope": "Legacy boundary of the org lifecycle and catalogue entry points (P01 F1) on disposable SQLite: the agent door's lifecycle tools and catalogue reads and the seven lifecycle operator routes. Turn delivery, the pre-archive interrupt, the remote reap, the transcript copy, manual compaction, provider discovery, the mail hub roster and the broadcasts are spies; the ledger, the doors, the receipts, save and reload are real. Legacy conformance evidence only: not a runtime census, not PostgreSQL or Rust qualification."
